  "answer": "To reduce the risk of image classifiers being forced to output wrong labels via small, imperceptible perturbations, adversarial training has been proposed (https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/NTwA3J99RPkgmp6jh/an-62-are-adversarial-examples-caused-by-real-but). The mechanism involves generating worst-case Lp-bounded perturbations (e.g., using Projected Gradient Descent) during each training step and including them in loss minimization; this suppresses the model's reliance on non-robust features and encourages it to focus on robust features instead (https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/NTwA3J99RPkgmp6jh/an-62-are-adversarial-examples-caused-by-real-but)."
